  <p>
    Industrial projects bring together structures, plant and site logistics that can be
    difficult to communicate through drawings. A physical model shows how the pieces fit
    together — the relationship between buildings, access routes, storage and open ground.
  </p>
  <p>
    We build models of factories, warehouses, plants and industrial facilities at a scale
    that keeps the whole site readable. Depending on the project, we can include access
    roads, hard standing, boundary treatment and simplified plant or equipment.
  </p>
  <p>
    These models are typically used for internal planning, approvals and stakeholder
    communication, where a clear physical overview saves time and avoids misunderstanding.
